// Your screens' effect gate. Scoped by the `includes` beside its entry in biome.jsonc.
//
// An effect syncs a component with something outside React. A read is not that, a call a person makes is not that,
// and going somewhere because of an answer is not that, so each has its own tool: `useRead` and `useAction` from
// `@pithy-sh/ui-core/src/read` and `src/action`, and the router's `<Redirect>`. An effect that really does sync with
// an outside system lives in a hook named for it, in its own file, and biome.jsonc excludes that file with the
// system it syncs with beside it — the screens `pithy ui add` writes ship four.
//
// This file is yours. Narrow the `includes` in biome.jsonc, widen them, or delete both the entry and this file.
language js

or {
  `useEffect($...)`,
  `useEffect<$_>($...)`,
  `useLayoutEffect($...)`,
  `useLayoutEffect<$_>($...)`,
  `$_.useEffect($...)`,
  `$_.useEffect<$_>($...)`,
  `$_.useLayoutEffect($...)`,
  `$_.useLayoutEffect<$_>($...)`
} as $call where {
  register_diagnostic(span=$call, message="A raw effect. Load data with useRead, run a call with useAction, navigate on an answer by rendering <Redirect>. An effect that syncs with something outside React goes in a hook named for it, in its own file, excluded in biome.jsonc.")
}
